    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nHi! Is there a way to define a custom textobject that will go from the current cursor position to the next closing quote?\r\n\r\nFor example, if I have the string \"hellothere\" and `|` is the cursor:\r\n\r\n`\"hello|there\"`\r\n\r\nIs there something I could set a textobject `Q` to such that typing `dQ` would result in:\r\n\r\n`\"hello\"`\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi! Is there a way to define a custom textobject that will go from the current cursor position to the next closing quote?</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For example, if I have the string \"hellothere\" and <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> is the cursor:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\"hello|there\"</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there something I could set a textobject <code class=\"notranslate\">Q</code> to such that typing <code class=\"notranslate\">dQ</code> would result in:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\"hello\"</code></p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nHi! Is there a way to define a custom textobject that will go from the current cursor position to the next closing quote?\nFor example, if I have the string \"hellothere\" and | is the cursor:\n\"hello|there\"\nIs there something I could set a textobject Q to such that typing dQ would result in:\n\"hello\"",
