                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "@krovuxdev Right, but I wanted to use mini.ai's wildcards like `q` to match _any_ quote. ex:\r\n\r\n`\"this is |a longer sentence\"` and `'this is |a longer sentence'`. using `dg]q` below as Evgeni mentioned works for this 😄 ",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/krovuxdev/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/krovuxdev\">@krovuxdev</a> Right, but I wanted to use mini.ai's wildcards like <code class=\"notranslate\">q</code> to match <em>any</em> quote. ex:</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\"this is |a longer sentence\"</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">'this is |a longer sentence'</code>. using <code class=\"notranslate\">dg]q</code> below as Evgeni mentioned works for this 😄</p>",
                    "bodyText": "@krovuxdev Right, but I wanted to use mini.ai's wildcards like q to match any quote. ex:\n\"this is |a longer sentence\" and 'this is |a longer sentence'. using dg]q below as Evgeni mentioned works for this 😄",
